    "title": "Final days before all 2,100 Aldi stores get green light to shut down for 24 hours",
    "text": "ALL Aldi stores across the US are set to close for 24 hours within a matter of days as the popular grocery chain marks a public holiday. Shoppers will need to look to other stores in the first weekend of April as every single Aldi store goes dark. Sign up for the Money newsletter Thank you! All US Aldi stores will close on Easter SundayCredit: Getty Aldi boasts more than 2,100 locations across 38 states. The chain only closes fully on four days a year: New Year’s Day, Easter Sunday, Thanksgiving Day, and Christmas Day. The grocery giant also has limited hours on Memorial Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Christmas Eve and New Year’s Eve. This year, Easter will fall next week on Sunday, April 5. Aldi will reopen on Monday at 8am in most locations across the US. Hours for your store can always be checked at its site locator. Many major retailers close all their locations to mark Easter Sunday meaning shoppers should make sure they have everything they need to avoid any last-minute emergencies. Costco, Target, and Kohl’s are among the other popular chains who will go dark for the holiday. Most read in Money USPS will also pause the majority of its mail services. Aldi has already caused a stir this Easter with a fun decorative item availabel for less than $10 going viral. The German supermarket’s Bunny Shaped Acacia Wood Board has taken the internet by storm. Made from durable acacia wood and shaped like a bunny, fans say it’s ideal for charcuterie boards and serving up a variety of snacks. Americans have already seen service and stores impacted by Presidents’ Day on February 16. USPS also paused its services on Martin Luther King Jr Day on January 19, as well as New Year’s Day on January 1. The next scheduled shutdown for many stores will be on Memorial Day on May 25. What holidays do mail and delivery services close for? USPS: New Year’s Day Martin Luther King, Jr. Day Presidents’ Day Easter Sunday Memorial Day Juneteenth Independence Day Labor Day Columbus Day Veterans Day Thanksgiving Day Christmas Day FedEx: Easter Sunday Independence Day Labor Day Thanksgiving Day Christmas Day New Year’s Day UPS: New Year’s Day Martin Luther King, Jr. Day Easter Mother’s Day Memorial Day Independence Day Labor Day Thanksgiving Day Christmas Day *** Some FedEx and UPS stores may be open on these holidays, while delivery and pickup services are unavailable. Consumers are urged to check their local stores’ hours. Comments",
